# Trivy exceptions for the dependency (trivy fs) scan (.github/workflows/trivy.yml).
#
# POLICY
#   - CRITICAL: always blocks the build, even if no fix is released. Ignoring a
#     CRITICAL here requires security-owner approval in the PR.
#   - HIGH: blocks only when a fix exists (unfixed HIGH is already bypassed by the
#     workflow, so it does NOT need an entry here).
#   - Do not add an entry just to get a build green. Prefer upgrading the base
#     dependency.
#
# EVERY ENTRY MUST HAVE
#   1. A comment line above it: why it is safe/not exploitable, who approved it,
#      and a link to the tracking issue.
#   2. An expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD, max ~90 days) so it is re-reviewed.
#
# FORMAT
#   # <justification> | approved by @user | <issue link>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# (no exceptions currently)
